issue_body:
Given the following FEA:

```fea
languagesystem DFLT dflt;
languagesystem latn dflt;

feature test {
    lookup alt1 {
	sub a by A;
    } alt1;
    lookup alt2 {
        sub b by B;
    } alt2;


    script latn;
    lookup alt1;

} test;
```

because `latn dflt` is one of the declared language systems, it inherits the two lookups that are declared at the top of the feature. The reference to `lookup alt1` under `latn` is redundant.

Currently, feaLib adds an extra lookup for this feature, even though it occurs earlier in the feature list. `makeotf` ignores the duplicate lookup, and the `latn/dflt` feature includes the two lookups inherited from `DFLT/dflt`.

I think that feaLib is incorrect here, although I'm not sure if this results in just slightly larger files, slightly less efficient shaping, or possibly errors in shaping?

(this test case is a reduction of an issue I found in about a hundred sources used by google fonts, so it may be worth some attention)

